; The room the registry's invariant binds to, and the instance the check stage
; reports against. It is canonical, so `dfcad fmt --check` passes over it, and it
; loads, so `dfcad check` runs the rule rather than refusing the model — which is
; what makes what follows a violation with a span on it rather than a diagnostic.
;
; The outline it names does not close. The annotation the gate places for it
; lands on the loop, in `geometry.dfc`, because the loop is the thing somebody
; has to change; the message names this room as the instance and the registry
; line the invariant is written at. Reading those two spans out of the result
; object is the whole of what the check stage's filter does.
(node
  site:S-002
  (label "Meeting Room B")
  (kind Space)
  (type MeetingRoom)
  (geometry area)
  (frame frame:building)
  (boundary geom:L-01))
